# OpenUI — required environment variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# MiniMax API (MiniMax) — REQUIRED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your API key at: https://platform.MiniMax.io/user-center/basic-information/interface-key
MINIMAX_API_KEY=sk-cp-your-key-here

# Optional: model to use (defaults to MiniMax-M3)
# Available models: MiniMax-M3, MiniMax-Text-01, etc.
MINIMAX_MODEL=MiniMax-M3

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public site origin — OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The absolute origin the app publishes about itself: metadataBase, the
# canonical link, the hreflang alternates, og:url. Resolved rather than
# required, because the right answer differs per environment.
#
# Order, first match wins:
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL          (this variable — production, or an override)
#   2. https://$VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL
#   3. https://$VERCEL_URL           (this deployment, so a preview describes itself)
#   4. http://localhost:${PORT:-3000}
#
# Leave it unset on Vercel and locally — the fallbacks are correct there. Set it
# when the site is served from a domain Vercel does not know about, or to point
# a local build at the production origin.
#
# A value that is set but is not an absolute http(s) URL fails loudly rather
# than falling through: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=english-course.online (no scheme)
# is a bug, not a hostname.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://english-course.online

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Course content storage — OPTIONAL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# WHERE each asset lives is declared in `content-locations.json`, not here:
# that file maps content keys to stores (local folder, S3 bucket, GCS bucket)
# and is tracked in git. The generated seed stores opaque content KEYS, so
# moving an asset between stores never regenerates seed-content.ts.
#
# These two variables are machine-scoped paths, not placement decisions.
#
# Where the location manifest is. Defaults to the repo root.
# CONTENT_LOCATIONS_PATH=content-locations.json
#
# Filesystem root the local driver reads bytes from (used by the notes reader
# and by existence checks). Relative paths resolve against the process CWD.
# CONTENT_LOCAL_ROOT=public/local-filesystem-lesson

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloud storage credentials — only when the manifest declares such a store
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never put credentials in content-locations.json; it is tracked in git.
# Bucket names, regions and CDN URLs are not secrets and belong there.
#
# AWS — read by the ambient credential chain (env, profile, or instance role).
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#
# Google Cloud — path to a service-account key, or use application-default
# credentials via `gcloud auth application-default login`.
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Draft courses — OPTIONAL, temporary
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# A course that declares "draft": true in its own manifest under src/content/
# is withheld from the served catalog: no card on the home, no continue-watching
# panel, and its URLs render the "We couldn't find this course" state. Today that
# is the Advanced Intermediate Course.
#
# Unset (the default) means drafts show whenever NODE_ENV is not "production",
# so `pnpm dev`, `pnpm test:run`, Storybook and the Playwright suite driving a
# dev server all see them with no configuration. A production build hides them.
#
# Accepted values: 1 / true to show, 0 / false to hide. Anything else fails
# loudly rather than being guessed at — SHOW_DRAFT_COURSES=treu is a bug, not
# a "no".
#
#   SHOW_DRAFT_COURSES=1   # review a draft course in a production build,
#                          # or run e2e against `pnpm build && pnpm start`
#   SHOW_DRAFT_COURSES=0   # check the production catalog locally
#
# To publish a course for good, delete its "draft": true line — no code change,
# no environment change. Removing this flag entirely is the recipe in
# openspec/changes/archive/2026-09-08-hide-draft-courses-in-production/design.md.
# SHOW_DRAFT_COURSES=
